            <ArticleTitle>An Unusual Case of Severe Stenosis of the Coronary Sinus Ostium in Association With Double Inlet Left Ventricle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>473-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/2150135114525646</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a patient with complex single ventricle physiology who was subsequently diagnosed with atresia of the coronary sinus ostium in the setting of myocardial dysfunction following operative palliation. Although a rare cardiac defect, awareness is important as the coronary venous system will often drain to a left superior vena cava (LSVC). If the LSVC is ligated without knowing of this defect, cardiac dysfunction and death can occur.</AbstractText>
